],"gloss":"golden ornaments"},{"surface":"பாண்டியன்","parts":[{"text":"பாண்டியன்","lemma":"pāṇṭiyaṉ","gloss":"Pandya king"}],"gloss":"Pandya king's"},{"surface":"வினைவலதிகன்","parts":[{"text":"வினை","lemma":"viṉai","gloss":"battle/deed"},{"text":"வல்","lemma":"val","gloss":"capable"},{"text":"அதிகன்","lemma":"atikaṉ","gloss":"Atikan"}],"gloss":"capable warrior Atikan"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"களிறொடு","parts":[{"text":"களிறு","lemma":"kaḷiṟu","gloss":"male elephant"},{"text":"ஒடு","lemma":"oṭu","gloss":"with"}],"gloss":"along with his male elephant"},{"surface":"பட்ட","parts":[{"text":"பட்ட","lemma":"பட்ட","gloss":"fell"}],"gloss":"fell","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"ஞான்றை","parts":[{"text":"ஞான்று","lemma":"ñāṉṟu","gloss":"time"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ai","gloss":"oblique/locative suffix"}],"gloss":"at the time when"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஒளிறு","parts":[{"text":"ஒளிறு","lemma":"oḷiṟu","gloss":"to shine"}],"gloss":"shining"},{"surface":"வாள்","parts":[{"text":"வாள்","lemma":"vāḷ","gloss":"sword"}],"gloss":"sword"},{"surface":"கொங்கர்","parts":[{"text":"கொங்கர்","lemma":"koṅkar","gloss":"Kongu people"}],"gloss":"Kongu warriors"},{"surface":"ஆர்ப்பினும்","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்ப்பு","lemma":"ārppu","gloss":"roar/shout"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"than"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even than the victory roar"},{"surface":"பெரிதே","parts":[{"text":"பெரிது","lemma":"peritu","gloss":"big/great"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"is far greater"}]}],"literal":"Intertwined flower garland to wilt, the chief / embraced days, those are few, but the gossip / at Vakai battlefield, where screech owls hoot, / when the Pandya king of golden ornaments, and his capable warrior Atikan, / fell along with his male elephant, / is louder than the victory roar of the Kongar with shining swords.","translation":"The days when the chief of the agricultural tract embraced me, making my intertwined flower garland wilt, were indeed very few. But the gossip about us is louder than the victory roar of the Kongar warriors with shining swords when Atikan, the capable commander of the Pandya king adorned with golden ornaments, fell along with his war elephant on the battlefield of Vākai where screech owls hoot.","modern":"நெருங்கிய மலர்மாலை வாடும்படியாகத் தலைவன் என்னைத் தழுவிய நாட்கள் மிகச் சிலவே. ஆனால், பசும்பொன் அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த பாண்டியனுடைய திறமைமிக்க வீரனாகிய அதிகன், கூகைகள் அலறும் வாகைப் பறந்தலை என்னும் போர்க்களத்தில் தன் ஆண் யானையோடு மடிந்தபோது, ஒளிரும் வாள்களை ஏந்திய கொங்கர்கள் எழுப்பிய ஆரவாரத்தை விடவும் எங்களைப் பற்றிய அலர் (வதந்தி) மிகப் பெரியதாகும்.","explanation":"This poem is spoken by the heroine's friend (tōḻi) to the heroine, or in the hearing of the hero, regarding the public gossip (alar) that has arisen in the town. The tiṇai is Marutam, which deals with the domestic discord and rumors surrounding the hero's infidelity and secret visits. The friend laments that the actual days of intimate union between the lovers were very few, yet the rumor spreading through the town is disproportionately massive. To emphasize the scale of this gossip, the poet Paraṇar employs a vivid historical allusion: the battle of Vākai, where the Pandya king's commander Atikan was slain along with his elephant, causing the victorious Kongu warriors to erupt in a deafening roar of triumph. The key words are 'makiḻnaṉ' (the lord of the agricultural tract), 'muyangiya' (embraced), 'alar' (gossip), and 'ārppu' (loud roar).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.9],[0.9,1.1],[1.1,1.4],[1.4,1.6],[1.6,2.4],[2.4,2.8],[2.9,3.3],[3.3,3.9],[3.9,4.5],[4.5,4.8],[4.8,5.13],[5.13,5.79],[5.79,6.5],[6.5,6.9],[6.9,7.17],[7.17,7.54],[7.54,7.9],[7.9,8.9],[8.9,9.2],[9.2,9.57],[9.57,9.82],[10.2,11.0],[11.0,11.3]],"female":[[0.0,1.1],[1.1,1.4],[1.4,1.8],[1.8,2.0],[2.0,3.2],[3.2,3.5],[3.6,4.0],[4.0,4.2],[4.2,4.72],[4.72,5.07],[5.07,5.59],[5.59,6.63],[6.63,7.5],[7.5,7.7],[7.9,8.2],[8.2,8.59],[8.59,9.33],[9.33,9.88],[9.88,10.44],[10.44,11.36],[11.36,12.1],[12.1,12.5],[12.5,13.0]]},"sync":[[["மயங்கு","intertwined"],["மலர்","flower"]],[["கோதை","garland"]],[["குழைய","to wilt"]],[["மகிழ்நன்","the chief"]],[["முயங்கிய","embraced"]],[["நாடவ","those days"],["சிலவே","are indeed few"]],[["சிலவே","are indeed few"]],[["அலரே","but the gossip"]],[["கூகை","screech owl"]],[["கோழி","fowl"]],[["வாகை","Vakai battlefield"],["பறந்தலை","battleground"]],[["பறந்தலை","battleground"]],[["பசும்பூண்","golden ornaments"]],[["பாண்டியன்","Pandya king's"]],[["வினைவலதிகன்","capable warrior Atikan"]],[["வினைவலதிகன்","capable warrior Atikan"]],[["களிறொடு","along with his male elephant"]],[["பட்ட","fell"]],[["ஞான்றை","at the time when"]],[["ஒளிறு","shining"],["வாள்","sword"]],[["கொங்கர்","Kongu warriors"]],[["ஆர்ப்பினும்","even than the victory roar"]],[["பெரிதே","is far greater"]]]}